{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAHP1Zd39g2XtCmQL66F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted **index 0** (Sb fraction 0.24, the most Pb-rich composition) as the best, but the evidence for it is weak. Every EQE I measured was essentially zero, and index 0 beat the others by less than the measurement noise.\n\n| Index | Sb fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 0.241 | 0.00288 |\n| 3 | 0.307 | 0.00192 |\n| 9 | 0.523 | 0.00229 |\n| 13 | 0.656 | −0.00108 |\n| 21 | 0.849 | 0.00192 |\n\n- **Why the line gave almost no signal:** my likely explanation is band gap. I expect the Pb antimonate compounds near these compositions (Pb₂Sb₂O₇ and PbSb₂O₆) to have band gaps too wide to absorb the 2.1 eV light used here.\n- **Why index 0:** Pb-rich films might contain some PbO, and one form of PbO (α-PbO) absorbs at about 1.9 eV. That would fit a small edge at this end, but I didn't confirm it.\n- **Budget used:** I spent all 5 EQE measurements, spread across the line to look for a peak, and did not use any of the 5 XRD measurements. So the phase explanations above are unconfirmed.\n- **Coverage gaps:** 24 of the 29 compositions were never measured. That includes indices 1–2, which lie between index 0 and index 3 on the Pb-rich side where the best reading came from."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":477,"cache_read_input_tokens":6734,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":477},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b407d67b-6941-46be-9911-6891753c9ffe","uuid":"c41e5770-4796-4bd7-a41b-38d286702732","timestamp":"2026-09-18T04:35:39.300Z","request_id":"req_011CfAHP1AoVdx8PKSJzuP85"}
